# el++ engine fixture 20 (src/test.slop: ksc-fixture-at, test-ksc-entailments).
# 20. The same merge through witnesses: Q1 ⊑ ∃r.(B ⊓ {a}) makes a a B
# only when Q1 is non-empty, so Q2 ⊑ ∃s.{a}, ∃s.B ⊑ E gives Q2 ⋢ E.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty . :t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:Q1 a owl:Class . :Q2 a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class .
:Q1 rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom [ owl:intersectionOf ( :B [ owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] ) ] ] .
:Q2 rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:hasValue :a ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :E .
